  "emphasis": {
    "primary": "Yin-Yang offense (Damage on three casts; self Increase Damage Given on Silent Rift and Yin-Yang Cascade)",
    "secondary": "Enemy exposure (Increase Damage Taken on Moonlit Inferno and Yin-Yang Cascade)",
    "tertiary": "Suppression (Decrease Damage Given on Moonlit Inferno)",
    "rationale": "Eight supported rows sit on four casts, and five of them are offensive: three 40-power Yin-Yang Damage rows (Silent Rift's ground circle, Yin-Yang Cascade, Silent Palm Strike) and two 35% self Increase Damage Given rows (Rift, Highest-filtered with no element; Cascade, Fire/Lightning/Yin-Yang/none) that both match the kit's own damage, stack on the caster and sit over a 25% + 0.15/level Increase Damage Given passive. The bloodline's Defensive and Control traits live in unsupported rows (seal on Silent Palm Strike, buffprevent/debuffprevent on Eternal Stillness, move on Silent Rift), so potency reaches control only through Moonlit Inferno's two 35% enemy debuffs (Decrease Damage Given and Increase Damage Taken, all four stat types, 40 AP) and Cascade's 35% exposure. Root Yang therefore carries the offense routes and root Yin the enemy-debuff routes; row-weighted full builds run 19–28 against the Taiyo Kami reference's 16–31."
  },
